// natural order; bit p of modeMask picks nad-L (zero the SUPER-diagonal [a1,a2], pivot A[a2,a2],
// b = -A[a1,a2]) vs pod (zero the SUB-diagonal [a2,a1], pivot A[a1,a1]) - both are LEFT rotations, i.e.
// real cube moves. Counts the non-identity rotations. modeMask == 0 reproduces the standard QR
// baseline. DESTRUCTIVE: consumes the passed matrix, so callers hand it a throw-away clone.

